#############################################
# Ithas Fire environment variables
#
# This file is intentionally a POINTER.
#
# Use the per-service templates instead:
# - API:    `apps/api/.env.example`   -> copy to `apps/api/.env`
# - Mobile: build-time values live in `apps/mobile/eas.json` (`build.<profile>.env`)
# - Infra:  `infra/docker/.env.example` -> copy to `infra/docker/.env`, read by docker-compose
#
# Most of what each app reads, with defaults and prod requirements, is in its
# env schema (`apps/api/src/lib/env.ts`, `apps/jobs/src/lib/env.ts`,
# `apps/web/src/config/env.server.ts` + `env.public.ts`). Some reads bypass the
# schemas (CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, DATABASE_SSL_*, ...); they are listed with the
# deployed values and traps in `docs/deploy.md#runtime-config-and-env-vars`.
#############################################
